    "self-hosting.data.arch_intro": "The browser reaches one Go process through an HTTPS reverse proxy; the process contains API, permissions, Agent, background jobs, UI and PocketBase. This is a diagram:",
    "self-hosting.data.arch_link": "View the architecture diagram",
    "self-hosting.data.kicker": "YOUR DATA, YOUR CONTROL",
    "self-hosting.data.point1_body": "One Go program contains the workbench, data service and migrations, run directly from the release package.",
    "self-hosting.data.point1_title": "Single-process delivery",
    "self-hosting.data.point2_body": "PocketBase/SQLite is embedded; the data directory and backups are operator-owned, and permission checks run server-side.",
    "self-hosting.data.point2_title": "Data stays in your environment",
    "self-hosting.data.point3_body": "Backups, recovery drills and upgrades are up to the deployer; the database does not roll back automatically.",
    "self-hosting.data.point3_title": "Backup and recovery responsibility",
    "self-hosting.data.title": "Apps and data stay in your control.",
